Z||000000||Sc00ter||09-21-2000||02:41 PM||||Okay, here's the problem, the thing idles kind rough. If I'm coasting it's fine, if I'm speeding up it's fine, but if I keep a constant speed it seems to skip. Replaced the O2 sensor and the EGR valve, still happening.<P>Any ideas?||||reg||9
Z||000001||1FST2M6||09-21-2000||03:23 PM||||welcome to the forum! um could be a host of things... is the distributor cap on tight? it may rattle at a constant speed and cause a misfiring condition but still idle.. (had a old 283 chevy in a truck that had that issue) or does it still perform well under WOT? (wide open throttle) if not check the fuel filter, and maybe a clogged injector. is it an automatic? might be a bad converter lock up solenoid... which Fiero is it?   hope this helps a bit...  ||||reg||1
